                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This short game is fun and leaves you wanting more. The story set in the future, the year 2273 when everything was covered with water and people starts to live in cities surrounded by a glass globe. 28 years later, a girl named Hope who lives in Pearl city, returned home and found out her father been missing for three days. She then decided to take a visit to his lab which he works in with another scientist. You'll discover many secrets and characters involving this disappearance. \n\nI enjoyed the puzzles in this game, they are unique and different from any other game I've played. One of them they gave you a pile of items and you have to replace them in their right place by checking the shadow (or dust) on the table. There are not many hidden objects scenes, but the few we have are very well made! \nhttps://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=1388758747\n\nThe art of this game is so pretty, especially the areas and the puzzles! There is a map but sadly there is no fast traveling option- however you can only explore an area at times, if you are in the apartment area, you'll only have two others rooms to explore, once you are done the game will automatically take you to the next area and the story will proceed which means there is no backtracking at all. the map looks nice. I've noticed that when you click on the hint button and the item you want is in another area, a small window will pop up for you to click and fast travel to that area. \nhttps://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=1389257497\nhttps://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=1388736728\n\nI didn't like the journal, although it gives objectives and is quite useful I have wished for it to keep the progress of the story and the backstory of the characters. The voice-over did a good job, music was fitting too\n\nPros:\n+Beautiful artwork.\n+Average story.\n+Well done voice over \n+Variety of puzzles.\n+Well drawn hidden object scenes. (But they are few)\n+Good soundtracks. \n\nCons:\n-No fast traveling map. (But there is no backtracking)\n-No journal.\n-Short game.\n-No steam achievements.\n\nIt took me two hours and a half to finish the game, quite short for its price so I recommend you get it on discount, they do pretty good discounts on steam. It is worth trying for casual gamers. I enjoyed the puzzles so much.\n\n[quote]𝐹𝑜𝑟 𝑚𝑜𝑟𝑒 𝑟𝑒𝑣𝑖𝑒𝑤𝑠 𝑐𝘩𝑒𝑐𝑘 𝑚𝑦 𝑐𝑢𝑟𝑎𝑡𝑜𝑟 𝑝𝑎𝑔𝑒 [url=http://store.steampowered.com/curator/32399565/]𝐹𝑒𝑒𝑛𝑎'𝑠 𝐶𝘩𝑜𝑖𝑐𝑒[/url][/quote]",
